          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most households, the Westinghouse iGen5000 is the electric start generator to buy: remote fob, inverter-quiet, and the right size for a refrigerator, sump pump and lights. In a cold climate, the fuel-injected Honda EU7000iS is worth its premium because it removes the choke from the cold-start routine, and if you need real 240V capacity on a budget, the Westinghouse WGen7500DFc brings remote start and a CO shutoff to home backup size.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whatever you buy, the start button is only as good as the battery behind it. Keep it on a maintainer, start the generator once a month, replace the battery on a schedule, and keep the recoil cord or a jump pack as your fallback.
          </p>
